From: vincek@netcom.com (Vince Kerchner)
Date: Mon, 24 Jan 1994 10:55:01 -0800
Subject: [#94-1-469] Meta: Prefixes (RFD)

Harry says:

>This is a request for discussion.
>
>In my view prefixes are great.

I agree.  I would prefer the continued (new?) use of subject line
prefixes for the following reasons:

1.  It makes human scanning of the posts much easier.

2.  It makes software filtering of the posts possible.

3.  Consistent use of prefixes (and the rest of the subject line)
    makes the digest contents smaller and easier to read.

4.  It makes automatic cataloging, indexing, and filing of posts
    possible sometime in the future (i.e. whenever there is software
    to support this).

I would even go so far as to suggest the use of hierarchical prefixes
so that different sub-threads of a thread can be maintained as part of
the main thread, e.g. "PREFIXES: GOOD: FILTERING: SOFTWARE: What I
wrote last weekend", etc...  The question here would be if people
could agree to use them consistently, and whether a prefix registry
(like Apple file types, creators, AppleEvents, etc...) was necessary.

