>This reminds me of our old discussion about reducing sleep time.  I have 
>done some research on sleep, but have never found an effective way to 
>reduce sleep.  Anybody on this list have any luck modifying their sleeping 
>habits?  If I could just gain a few hours per day without any bad 
>side-effects, this would be a tremendous help.

I require about 8 hours sleep per day if it is all taken at once.  However,
for a period of about 3 months, I was able to function as well or better on
6 hours per day by breaking it into 2 parts: 4 hours at night (10P-2A), and
2 hours in the afternoon (~2P-4P).  I was alert and energetic, but also
noticed increased creativity because I was always closer to that dream
state where many of my good ideas come from.  If my work ever allows, I
will try it again, some day.

